    "image_with_text_jzjctF": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_raakbm": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Q: </strong>You often repurpose heirloom pieces for clients. What is it like holding something that already carries history and turning it into something new?</p><p><strong>A: </strong>It’s exciting to meet each client and share their touching stories and histories associated with each legacy piece, even if it is broken or unwearable. I’m blessed to be part of their journey to create something that can be worn again as a unique heirloom, a celebration of something new, or a legacy piece that can be passed on to another generation. Each individual piece of repurposed jewelry is a reminder of past relationships, associations and emotional bridges. But most importantly, hope for the future that draws from a personal past.  </p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "text_raakbm"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_2760.jpg",
        "height": "adapt",
        "desktop_image_width": "medium",
        "layout": "image_first",
        "desktop_content_position": "middle",
        "desktop_content_alignment": "left",
        "content_layout": "no-overlap",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-1",
        "mobile_content_alignment": "left",
        "padding_top": 0,
        "padding_bottom": 36
      }
    },
    "image_with_text_chmGqr": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_hwefqz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Q: </strong>Nature seems to play a role in your work. What does a walk outside give you creatively?</p><p><strong>A: </strong>I think the smell, feel and touch of nature that surrounds me nurture my creativity. It’s not like I have to replicate nature, but translating the very sense of emotions that I gather into my jewelry designs represents my most challenging reward.  As an artist, I’m a story teller and translator for Mother Nature.</p><p><strong>Q:</strong> How would you describe your personal style? Any items in your closet you can’t live without?</p><p><strong>A: </strong>I think my personal style is comfort and simple design.  Easy layering and basic colors that can be changed to adapt to each season.  I love wearing a red linen blouse in spring or summer and a red sweater for the winter!</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "text_hwefqz"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_2759_ccdd0a19-5ba4-4cb4-948f-4b0fec1371c9.jpg",
        "height": "adapt",
        "desktop_image_width": "medium",
        "layout": "text_first",
        "desktop_content_position": "middle",
        "desktop_content_alignment": "left",
        "content_layout": "no-overlap",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-1",
        "mobile_content_alignment": "left",
        "padding_top": 0,
