      }
    },
    "image_with_text_i9eTWE": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_F8A8Hp": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Q: </strong>What feels exciting right now? Any materials, shapes or stories you want to explore next?</p><p><strong>A: </strong>For the past 40 plus years of making jewelry, I have been living and travelling to different parts of the world.  I love collecting different stones from all over the place, especially old jade pieces that I have amassed too much of in my material drawers. I’m excited that I can create pieces that speak to me.  I often go through an iterative process of pulling out my collections of stones, where they then sit on my bench for a while until a certain thought crystallizes and inspires me to turn them into pendants, rings or something special. Circular, square or triangle are often the shapes that attract me. I can never predict each time I sit down at my bench what mental process occurs. This uncertainty and spontaneity is the reason why I still love creating jewelry.</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
